 "name": "Fazenda: rain look (Rain colour 2026-11-14)",
 "notes": "Every day colour name used here -> its rainy colour: the Lagoa house's rain shift (lh_snapshot/looks.rain_formula: each colour keeps its day hue and at least its day chroma, greens 24% richer and deeper with bright glossy highlights, lightness about 12-20% lower, a soft blue-teal sky light that cools the neutrals), plus wet earth on the paths (dirt -> one step muddier, then the shift). Outdoor = the full shift; indoor = the same shift at half strength. Look colours (exact formula values, like the night twins), not pack palette entries. 'sheen' = wet highlights on stone and boards; 'extra' = rain-only colours (the blue-violet overcast rn_sky0-2 in puddles and on the cove, rn_glint for the falls, drops and whitecaps, rn_mist for the jungle mist).",
